        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            For a homeowner coating their own garage, RockSolid Polycuramine is the best all-round choice: tougher and quicker to return to service than standard epoxy, and available off the shelf. EpoxyShield is the value option for sound slabs and moderate use, ArmorPoxy suits heavy workshops, a one-part paint suits storage spaces, and a penetrating sealer is the safe answer for slabs with moisture issues.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            If you want the most durable floor and have the budget, a professional polyaspartic system is still the benchmark. Whatever you choose, check the slab first. Moisture, old coatings and oil stains decide whether any coating bonds, and an hour of testing is worth more than any upgrade on the label.
          </p>
        </div>

